# ingress-nginx — Pulumi -> ArgoCD platform cutover (LEAF networking component).
#
# !!! CRITICAL — NOT CURRENTLY LIVE ON dev-local !!!
# This component is DEAD on the live cluster and the values below mirror the
# Pulumi *intended* spec (pkg/applications/ingress.go), NOT a running release.
# Verified on-cluster (2026-06-20, KUBECONFIG=~/.kube/cluster.yaml):
#   * `helm get values ingress-nginx -n ingress-nginx -a`  -> "release: not found"
#   * no `ingress-nginx` namespace, deployment, pod, svc, or helm secret exist
#   * the ONLY IngressClass is `traefik` (k3s built-in, controller
#     traefik.io/ingress-controller, in kube-system; releases traefik +
#     traefik-crd) — Traefik is the real ingress controller on this cluster.
# Root cause: main.go:61 resolves
#   ingressEnabled := pulumiConf.GetBool("ingress_controller_enabled", false)
# default=false, and Pulumi.local.yaml never sets it true, so the call at
# main.go:217-218 (DeployIngressController) is never invoked.
# (`ingress:namespace: ingress-nginx` in the stack config is only a namespace
# string, not an enable flag. ingress.go's own internal default GetBool(...,true)
# is unreachable because main.go gates the call with default=false.)
#
# OWNERSHIP HANDOFF: NONE. Pulumi never created any ingress-nginx objects, so
# there is no helm-release ownership for ArgoCD to adopt. If adopted, this is a
# greenfield install — no `pulumi up`/disable-flag handoff is required (unlike a
# truly-live component). Keep ingress_controller_enabled=false in Pulumi so it
# never competes for ownership.
#
# DECISION REQUIRED before applying this ApplicationSet:
#   (a) Do NOT introduce ingress-nginx — keep Traefik as the cluster ingress and
#       drop this file (preferred unless there's a concrete need); OR
#   (b) Intentionally adopt ingress-nginx as a NEW component — then this is a
#       greenfield install (no Pulumi ownership to hand off) and you must decide
#       how it coexists with Traefik (two IngressClasses; ingress-nginx will NOT
#       be cluster default unless you set controller.ingressClassResource.default).
#
# Values below mirror ingress.go exactly (controller.service.type=ClusterIP,
# controller.resources.requests cpu=100m/memory=90Mi). targetRevision pins the
# chart version from ingress.go (4.7.1). If adopting fresh, consider bumping to a
# current 4.x — 4.7.1 (Aug 2023) is old; pin deliberately.
apiVersion: argoproj.io/v1alpha1
kind: ApplicationSet
metadata:
  name: ingress-nginx
  namespace: argocd
  labels:
    environment: ingress-nginx
spec:
  goTemplate: true
  goTemplateOptions: ["missingkey=zero"]
  generators:
    - clusters: {}
  template:
    metadata:
      name: ingress-nginx
      labels:
        app: ingress-nginx
      annotations:
        # Leaf networking component: install after operators/issuers/CRDs
        # (negative waves) but before app workloads. The chart bundles its own
        # CRDs, so no separate CRD wave is needed.
        argocd.argoproj.io/sync-wave: "1"
    spec:
      project: platform-project
      source:
        repoURL: https://kubernetes.github.io/ingress-nginx
        chart: ingress-nginx
        targetRevision: "4.7.1"
        helm:
          version: v3
          values: |
            controller:
              service:
                type: ClusterIP
              resources:
                requests:
                  cpu: 100m
                  memory: 90Mi
      destination:
        server: '{{.server}}'
        namespace: ingress-nginx
      syncPolicy:
        automated:
          prune: true
          selfHeal: true
        syncOptions:
          - CreateNamespace=true
